# Brief: Update the Fodda Website Claude Integration Page

## Context

When a user asks Claude to "connect to a PSFK or Fodda knowledge graph," Claude gives them generic instructions but can't provide the specific URL. If the user then visits the Fodda website's Claude page (`fodda.ai/#/platform-integration-anthropic-claude`), they find an enterprise-focused page about plugin manifests, CORS, and OIDC — nothing that helps a regular Claude Pro/Max user paste a URL into Settings → Connectors.

The page needs to serve **two audiences**:
1. **Individual users** (Claude Pro / Max / Team) who want to add Fodda as a custom connector in ~60 seconds
2. **Enterprise admins** (Claude Enterprise) who need admin-managed connector registration, security details, and compliance info

---

## Current State

The page (`IntegrationClaude.tsx`) currently:
- ✅ Has a good hero and "What This Integration Does" section
- ✅ Lists capabilities (search, neighbors, evidence, node fetch)
- ❌ "How It Works" section is developer/enterprise-only (manifest hosting, CORS, OIDC)
- ❌ Never shows the actual URL: `https://mcp.fodda.ai/mcp`
- ❌ "Getting Started" steps are enterprise-centric (host manifest, configure CORS, etc.)
- ❌ FAQ says "Yes — enterprise plugin support is required" (this is wrong — any Claude Pro/Max/Team user can add custom connectors)
- ❌ No mention of MCP or the connector flow that Claude web users actually use

---

## Proposed Changes

### Change 1: Add a "Connect in 60 Seconds" Section

Add a prominent, user-friendly section **immediately after the hero** (before "What This Integration Does"). This should be the highest-visibility element on the page.

**Content:**

```
## Connect Fodda to Claude in 60 Seconds

Works with Claude Pro, Max, Team, and Enterprise plans.

Step 1: Get your API key
  → Sign up or log in at app.fodda.ai
  → Go to Account → MCP Integration
  → Copy your API key

Step 2: Add Fodda as a connector in Claude
  → In Claude, go to Settings → Connectors → Add custom connector
  → Paste this URL:

     https://mcp.fodda.ai/mcp        [Copy button]

  → Set auth to "Custom request headers"
  → Add header: Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY

Step 3: Start asking questions
  → "What are the latest retail trends?"
  → "Show me beauty innovation signals with evidence"
  → "What brands are driving the wellness space?"

Claude will query your Fodda knowledge graph directly and return 
grounded answers with traceable sources.
```

Include a **Copy URL** button and a **Get Started** CTA linking to `app.fodda.ai`.

Design this section with a dark card background (like the existing "Why It Matters" section) to make it visually distinct and immediately actionable.

